anaksor-ocr
Copyright 2026 Sokheng Din

The networks in src/anaksor/nets are written for anaksor from the papers they implement
(DBNet, RepViT, SVTRv2, SMTR, CPPD; see README.md). Their layer layout and tensor names follow
the OpenOCR implementations (https://github.com/Topdu/OpenOCR, Apache License 2.0) that
the released models were trained with, so those checkpoints load unchanged.

Khmer name recognition model: Sokheng Din, anaksor-ocr rec-svtrv2-v4.
Upstream model and character dictionary (Apache License 2.0):
https://huggingface.co/Sokheng/anaksor-ocr/tree/5518ec408419be074e8214712c673d41ffa84285
The bundled ONNX graph applies dynamic INT8 quantization to constant MatMul
and Gemm weights. The character dictionary is unchanged.
